Z||000000||Seanh||04-27-2001||08:32 PM||||I found another Fiero in town today. It is a very nice and well taken care of 85 GT. Color is silver, and it pretty much matches my 86 GT perfectly with the exception of the body style. I went in to ask what they wanted for it (used dealership) and they told me $5500. I asked if they were smoking crack or what. They said straight faced they were asking $5500. It has 80K miles on it, and it's overall in great condition, but I think that price is a litle high. What do you think? Is it really that high? Any idea on what I should offer to them for it? I would really like to have it, but woundn't pay more then $3500 for it. Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||04-27-2001||08:38 PM||||If they have a 3 year 50,000 mile bumper to bumper warrenty on it, it worth $5500, other wise a cherry 85 GT may bring $3500.<P>Give them your name and number and have them call you when they get real.||||reg||1
